# Built site output. The deploy workflow rebuilds ./public from source with
# `hugo --minify` and publishes it to the separate pablobernabeu.github.io repo,
# so a committed copy here is redundant build output (it was ~1.5 GB / 3,000+
# files bloating history). Kept out of tracking; still generated on disk locally.
/public/
# API keys and secrets (never commit — keys belong in GitHub Actions secrets)
**/scopus_key.txt
**/Scopus API key.txt
**/Scopus*key*.txt

# Transient Scopus search snapshots. Citations are durable in
# related-references.html and unfinished candidates in pending-dois.json; these
# timestamped dumps were re-created on every scheduled run and reached
# 5,115 files / 62 MB before being dropped from tracking. Matched by filename
# because the containing directory is spelled both "related references" and
# "related-references".
content/publication/**/DOIs, *.csv
content/publication/**/additional DOIs, *.csv
content/publication/**/date and time of previous retrieval of DOIs.txt

# blogdown lock files. These are transient guards left behind by an interrupted
# render, but blogdown treats any that it finds as "a render is in progress" and
# silently skips the post. One was committed in 2024 and blocked rebuilds of
# content/post/speculation-across-various-scientific-topics for two years.
*.Rmd.lock~

